{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;By reasons of the substandard width of the double bedroom in Flat 1, the lack of direct access to rear garden for first floor flat and adverse noise impact from vertical stacking issues would cumulatively result in sub-standard level of living accommodation for the future occupiers of the proposed dwellings, contrary to Policies D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), Technical housing standards – nationally described space standard (2015), Housing Design Standards London Plan Guidance (2023) and Harrow Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Insufficient information has been submitted to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority that the proposed development would be resistant and resilient to surface water flooding contrary to policies SI 12 of the London Plan (2021) and DM9 of the Harrow Development Management Policies (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;By reasons of the lack of evidence to demonstrate that the proposed vehicle crossover would have no damage to existing street trees and a lack of soft landscaping features on the front garden and the proposal would adversely diminish the public grass verges on the pavement, the proposal would detract from the existing suburban character of the streetscene and the wider area which fails to contribute to streetside greenery contrary to policies G7 of the London Plan (2021) and policies DM22 and DM23 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed vehicle crossover via Belmont Road would be in close proximity to the existing road junction which would not ensure safe access for the future occupants of the proposed development, nor the safe and free flow of the public highway. The proposed on-site parking spaces would also exceed the maximum standards set out in Table 10.3 of the London Plan which would discourage active modes and public transport, contrary to policies T4, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021) and polices DM42 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
